33512.sol:
Let given expansion be

$\begin{aligned}$&$\mathrm{S}=($1+x)^{1000}+x(1+x)^{999}+x² \\
&(1+x)^{998}+\ldots+\ldots+x^{1000}
\end{aligned}

Put $1+x=t\mathrm{S}=$t^{1000}+x t^{999}+x²(t)^{998}+\ldots+x^{1000}

This is a G.P$ with common ratio\frac{x}{t} \begin{aligned}\mathrm{S}$&=$\frac{t^{1000}\left[1-\left(\frac{x}{t}\right)^{1001}\right]}{1-\frac{x}{t}}$\\
&=$\frac{(1+x)^{1000}\left[1-\left(\frac{x}{1+x}\right)^{1001}\right]}{1-\frac{x}{1+x}}$\\
=& $\frac{(1+x)^{1001}\left[(1+x)^{1001}-x^{1001}\right]}{(1+x)^{1001}}
\end{aligned}

=\left[($1+x)^{1001}-x^{1001}\right]

Now coeff$ of x^{50}$ in above expansion is equal to coeff of $x^{50} in (1+x)^{1001}$ which is $\binom{1001}{50}=\frac{(1001) !}{50 !(951) !}$

